					<description><![CDATA[<p>Funding Accelerates Directed-Energy Defence Expansion  Aurelius Systems raises $40 million in Series A for growth The company plans to use capital to increase manufacturing, expand operations and support U.S.-based supply</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/aurelius-systems-raises-40m-to-advance-autonomous-defense-platform/" data-wpel-link="internal">Aurelius Systems Raises $40M To Advance Autonomous Defense Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Funding Accelerates Directed-Energy Defence Expansion</b><span style="font-weight: 400"> </span></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Aurelius Systems raises $40 million in Series A for growth The company plans to use capital to increase manufacturing, expand operations and support U.S.-based supply chain as demand for high-performance counter-drone solutions rises. </span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Draper Associates and KAS Venture Partners co-led the round, joined by General Catalyst, Hanwha Defense USA, Outlander, Alumni Ventures, Bravo Victor Venture Capital, Detroit Venture Partners, Decisive Point and more.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The new investment reflects growing demand for autonomous defence technologies as governments increase spending on counter-drone capabilities. Defence organisations are seeking systems that can respond quickly to evolving aerial threats while reducing operational costs and improving mission readiness. </span></p>
<h2><b>Aurelius Systems Expands Archimedes Platform</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding will accelerate technical development and increase production capacity for Aurelius&#8217; flagship Archimedes defence platform. Aurelius also plans vertical integration strengthening manufacturing readiness while reducing long-term supply chain disruption risks significantly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The strategy improves access to essential materials supporting reliable manufacturing and future production expansion across defence markets. Beyond Archimedes, the company plans expanding its product portfolio while entering additional defence industry market segments globally.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Chief executive Michael LaFramboise said coordinated drone attacks have fundamentally changed today&#8217;s modern defence landscape worldwide significantly. He said Archimedes was designed as a scalable platform protecting people, infrastructure, assets, and critical defence targets.</span></p>
<h2><b>AI And Directed Energy Drive Defence Innovation</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">San Francisco-based Aurelius Systems develops artificial intelligence-powered sensing, robotics, and directed-energy systems for autonomous aerial defence. Its technologies detect, track, and defeat aerial threats without requiring continuous human intervention during active operations worldwide.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Archimedes is an autonomous laser-based counter-drone system designed to protect military forces and critical infrastructure from attacks. The platform offers faster response times and lower operating costs than many conventional air defence systems today.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its autonomous directed-energy technology provides continuous protection against increasingly sophisticated and rapidly evolving </span><a href="https://builtin.com/drones" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">drone</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> threats worldwide effectively. Draper Associate, Andy Tang praised Aurelius for demonstrating core technologies and building strategic deployment partnerships successfully.</span></p>
<h2><b>Recent Milestones Strengthen Growth Strategy</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204070" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204070" class="size-full wp-image-204070" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/Aurelius-2.png" alt="Illustration of an autonomous directed-energy defence platform integrated with AI command-and-control systems, manufacturing expansion, and strategic defence partnerships." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204070" class="wp-caption-text">Recent operational milestones, strategic partnerships, and successful defence testing are strengthening confidence in autonomous directed-energy platforms as manufacturing and deployment capabilities continue to expand. Source: Created by Ventureburn.</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding follows several important operational milestones for Aurelius. He said those achievements position Aurelius leading autonomous directed-energy systems from concept through commercial deployment and adoption.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company recently formed an integration partnership with American Rheinmetall to expand deployment opportunities for the Archimedes platform. It also completed interoperability testing with command-and-control systems during Operation Jailbreak and successfully validated its platform during the Technology Readiness Experimentation (T-REX) 26-2 programme.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">These achievements have strengthened confidence in the platform&#8217;s readiness for future defence deployments while supporting continued investment in manufacturing capabilities. Aurelius currently employs 19 people and expects to grow its workforce to more than 40 employees before the end of 2026 as production scales.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/faye-raises-50m-series-c-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Faye Raises $50M In Series C To Expand AI Travel Protection Platform</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Investment Supports Manufacturing And Market Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The Series A funding positions Aurelius to increase production while supporting long-term manufacturing resilience in the United States. The company is investing in domestic supply chain infrastructure alongside strategic partnerships to improve delivery timelines and reduce dependence on external suppliers.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">As autonomous aerial threats become more common across military and critical infrastructure environments, Aurelius aims to provide scalable AI-powered defensive systems that can be deployed rapidly across multiple sectors.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The latest investment provides the resources needed to expand the company&#8217;s manufacturing footprint, strengthen its technology platform, and accelerate customer deliveries as the market for autonomous defence technologies continues to grow.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/aurelius-systems-raises-40m-to-advance-autonomous-defense-platform/" data-wpel-link="internal">Aurelius Systems Raises $40M To Advance Autonomous Defense Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
