					<description><![CDATA[<p>Convex Raises $57M To Advance AI Backend Infrastructure Convex has raised $57 million in Series B funding and plans to utilize the new capital to scale development on its AI-native</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/convex-raises-57m-series-b/" data-wpel-link="internal">Convex Raises $57M To Build Reliable AI-Native Backend Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<h2><b>Convex Raises $57M To Advance AI Backend Infrastructure</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex has raised $57 million in Series B funding and plans to utilize the new capital to scale development on its AI-native backend platform. Insight Partners led the financing round, which included a contribution from Etna Labs and all previous investors a16z, and Spark Capital.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With the Series B, Convex has raised $110.5 million of total funding-it says it will use the cash to mature its core platform, improve its agentic development tooling, and grow its staffing levels at its San Francisco-headquartered business.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex-which was founded in 2021 by former Dropbox infrastructure engineers-provides a fully-integrated backend platform for developers, combining databases, functions, workflows, search, synchronization, authentication and file storage in a single platform built for software development.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The funding round is part of a trend to AI-assisted coding and autonomous development tooling, and Convex thinks developers need an infrastructure that scales their application&#8217;s complexity while maintaining high reliability.</span></p>
<h2><b>Platform Targets Reliable AI-Generated Applications</p>
<p></b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex believes traditional backend infrastructure struggles to support the growing use of AI coding agents. According to the company, AI-generated applications built on conventional databases can silently introduce data errors that only appear after deployment.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company said internal testing found that 90% of AI-built applications running on traditional databases experienced data corruption during real-world use. By comparison, applications built on Convex&#8217;s platform completed the same tests without failures.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Its backend includes built-in ACID transactions, end-to-end type safety, real-time subscriptions, and TypeScript support. These features reduce the need for developers to manually integrate multiple services while improving application reliability.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex also packages search capabilities, workflow automation, authentication, file storage, and retrieval-augmented generation features that extend AI applications with organisation-specific knowledge.</span></p>
<h2><b>Customer Base Continues To Grow<br />
</b></h2>
<div id="attachment_204027" style="width: 1322px" class="wp-caption alignnone"><img decoding="async" aria-describedby="caption-attachment-204027" class="size-full wp-image-204027" src="https://ventureburn.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/a-vibrant-futuristic-poster-depicts-a-sp__JVLeiopVhKvK3C92UPi0A_2hRrQ5_nRzCD4c40bPlpnA.png" alt="A neon futuristic visual showing AI-powered backend systems supporting large-scale application development." width="1312" height="736" /><p id="caption-attachment-204027" class="wp-caption-text">Convex powers scalable and reliable backend infrastructure for AI-driven applications worldwide. Source: Created by Ventureburn</p></div>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The platform has gained significant adoption among developers building AI-powered software. Convex now supports nearly two million applications created by almost 500,000 developers worldwide. The company also reported more than 1.2 million weekly npm downloads.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Customers include OpenAI, Tripadvisor, Solana, Zapier, and Reducto. These organisations use Convex to simplify backend development while supporting applications that require dependable performance at scale.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Insight Partners said the growing use of AI coding assistants has exposed weaknesses in traditional software infrastructure. The investment firm believes Convex offers developers a more reliable foundation where backend components work together without extensive configuration.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">More News: </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/delightree-raises-25m-funding/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">Delightree Raises $25M To Expand AI Operating System For Franchise Businesses</span></a></p>
<h2><b>Funding Supports Product Innovation And Expansion</b></h2>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Convex plans to use the new funding to accelerate product innovation as AI transforms software engineering. Convex will fund new tools simplifying application development for developers and artificial intelligence agents building software.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">The company will continue providing highly reliable </span><a href="https://community.d2l.com/brightspace/kb/articles/25616-products-backend" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener external noreferrer" data-wpel-link="external"><span style="font-weight: 400">backend products</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> supporting increasingly complex artificial intelligence-powered applications worldwide. Convex believes stable backend infrastructure becomes increasingly essential as artificial intelligence generates larger amounts of application code.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">Instead of combining separate components, Convex provides one unified platform reducing complexity and preventing software bugs efficiently. The funding will strengthen Convex&#8217;s engineering team while expanding its global developer ecosystem and platform capabilities significantly.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">With fresh capital and a growing customer base, Convex aims to strengthen its position in the emerging AI development infrastructure market by making reliable software engineering faster and easier for both human developers and AI agents.</span></p>
<p><span style="font-weight: 400">To stay updated on crypto venture capital funding and market trends, visit our </span><a href="https://ventureburn.com/category/news/venture-capital/" data-wpel-link="internal"><span style="font-weight: 400">venture capital news section</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400"> for more insights.</span></p>
<p>The post <a href="https://ventureburn.com/convex-raises-57m-series-b/" data-wpel-link="internal">Convex Raises $57M To Build Reliable AI-Native Backend Platform</a> appeared first on <a href="https://ventureburn.com" data-wpel-link="internal">Ventureburn</a>.</p>
]]></content:encoded>
					
		
		
